    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27364" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyctus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> ,
			i, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λύκτος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Crete, east of Gnossus, a colony of the
				Lacedæmonians</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 7,
				12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12, 20, §
			59</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyctĭus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to
				Lyctus, Lyctian, Cretan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lyctius Idomeneus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 401</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">classis,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the Cretan</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 490</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
